  This is the discriminator: the one benchmark whose fuel is both thermal
  and strongly self-shielded in the U-238 resolved resonances. Measured
  2026-09-11 at 10 000 × [250 + 400]: k = 1.02950 ± 0.00061, i.e.
  +2950 ± 61 pcm — against +4004 pcm on the FHR pebble, and against the
  +3200 pcm predicted by carrying that pebble's 11 % resonance-integral
  deficit onto p ≈ 0.75. The residual is this code's self-shielded U-238
  resonance absorption, reproduced on a measured critical experiment; it
  is not the pebble's reference deck. NOTE: the resonance attribution is
  REFUTED by --case 2 and --case 8; see the module docs.
